:1609442062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-02-24T10:06:18Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T08:35:19Z","closed_at":"2026-08-14T08:31:02Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Not reproducible in 4.5\n- Reproducible in 4.6 & 4.6.1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9144) - AMD Ryzen 9 5950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 63.94 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn Godot 4.5 and previous, visual shader resource files inlcuded the generated shader code.\n\nThis can be used to automatically generate strongly typed `get/set_shader_parameter` for shaders.\n\nIn 4.6 and 4.6.1, the shader no longer includes the generated code, so this can't be done (without writing a parser for the visual shader)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a visual shader in 4.5, save as resource, upgrade to 4.6 and modify it. The shader code will be deleted.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nAttached is a shader pre and post 4.6.\n\n[VisualShaderIssue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25516110/VisualShaderIssue.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Seb105","id":65898127,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODk4MTI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65898127?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Seb105","html_url":"https://github.com/Seb105","followers_url":"https:/